dms-glass: minimal QML patch for DankMaterialShell (base: v1.6.2, .dankrev 3f15ae07e999b609)
Applied by ~/.local/bin/dms-glass-build onto a copy of the embedded DMS UI tree
(patch -p1 --fuzz=0; the build fails loudly if any hunk no longer applies).
Launched by ~/.local/bin/dms-glass-run (falls back to stock `dms run` when stale).

Why: settings.json alone leaves these nested surfaces near-opaque:
  - notification-centre cards: painted twice at popupTransparency (Rectangle + ElevationShadow fill)
    -> measured 0.857 over the panel (0.95 of the backdrop hidden). Now one fill at foregroundLayerTransparency.
  - spotlight search field: alpha floor 0.74 -> now foregroundLayerTransparency.
  - clipboard history rows: popupTransparency over a popupTransparency panel -> now Theme.nestedSurface.
Every changed line carries a "dms-glass" comment so a rebase is easy to audit.

--- a/Common/Theme.qml
+++ b/Common/Theme.qml
@@ -477,7 +477,8 @@
     readonly property color notepadWindowSurface: withAlpha(surfaceContainer, notepadTransparency)
     readonly property color nestedSurface: floatingSurfaceHigh
     readonly property color notificationFloatingSurface: notificationForegroundLayers ? readableSurface : withAlpha(readableSurface, 0)
-    readonly property color notificationFloatingSurfaceHigh: notificationForegroundLayers ? readableSurfaceHigh : withAlpha(readableSurfaceHigh, 0)
+    // dms-glass: notification cards use the foreground-layer alpha like every other nested card (stock: popupTransparency)
+    readonly property color notificationFloatingSurfaceHigh: notificationForegroundLayers ? withAlpha(surfaceContainerHigh, foregroundLayerTransparency) : withAlpha(surfaceContainerHigh, 0)
     readonly property color notificationNestedSurface: notificationFloatingSurfaceHigh
     readonly property real blurLayerOutlineOpacity: Math.max(0, Math.min(1, typeof SettingsData === "undefined" ? 0.12 : (SettingsData.blurLayerOutlineOpacity ?? 0.12)))
